From dac3ce3891f9d6f97015f0eb07aa2b19593609cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:51:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVDOverlayCodecFFmpeg: Automatic guesses nothing in an SDR
 video (subtitles.hadesbitmaprange)

In Automatic, a PGS stream in an SDR video was taken as made for HDR when its brightest text was
neutral and at the light of HDR text (Y' 115 to 165). That is also the light of SDR text of a middle
grey: a grey made at 60 % in an SDR video would have been drawn white, a picture that came out right
changed on a guess. Fidelity comes first: Automatic now tells one thing only, and only where it is
certain. In a PQ video, a mostly opaque palette entry with a Y' of 202 or more is made for SDR (as PQ
it would be over 2000 cd/m2, and no subtitle is made for HDR that bright), and the stream is drawn as
SDR. In an SDR video nothing is read and nothing is guessed: the stream is SDR as its video, as in
Kodi; PGS made for HDR in an SDR video, which look grey, are set with the choice HDR, which stays.

With Automatic and an SDR video the codec does what it did before this setting: its palettes are
decoded with the video's matrix (the codec's colorspace is changed only where a palette tells SDR in a
PQ video, or a choice is fixed) and the overlays are not HDR overlays (m_isHDROverlay is the range,
SDR as the video). The help of "Bitmap subtitles made for" says so in en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx,
and kodi.log says, when a PGS stream opens in an SDR video, that nothing is guessed there.

Tests (outside the tree): pgs_range_test: every one of the 2926 real packets of the two Ultra HD
Blu-ray remuxes, and every synthetic palette (SDR text of every colour, HDR white at 60 to 500
cd/m2), in an SDR video with Automatic tells nothing and leaves the stream SDR as its video; in a PQ
video the Transformers track is still told SDR and the 42 tracks of Tron: Legacy stay HDR; mutants
(guessing in an SDR video, telling PQ, the threshold, the alpha, the once, the reading of the
segments) each caught. pgs_wiring.py range: the colorspace of the codec is set only by a fixed choice
or by a palette that tells it.
